content:
The cuboid is \(3\) cubes wide, \(3\) cubes high, and \(2\) cubes deep.

1. The dark piece has a vertical run of three cubes at the front-right corner (including the orange-outlined lower cube).
2. On the right face, another dark cube is visible at the back-bottom corner.
3. The two cubes immediately to the left of this back-bottom cube are completely hidden from the front, top, and right views.

Thus the dark piece forms the chain
\[
\text{three cubes vertically}
\;\longrightarrow\;
\text{one cube backward}
\;\longrightarrow\;
\text{two cubes leftward}.
\]

This is exactly the structure of Shape C and can be obtained by rotation without reflection. The other shapes either require a dimension of \(4\), or would make additional light-colored cubes appear dark.

\[
\boxed{\text{C: Shape C}}
\]
